# INSTALL
# The first install only: what to do next (an update needs no reminder).
case "$ACTION" in
post)
	# External screens' brightness over DDC/CI needs i2c-dev now, not only
	# from the next boot (usr/lib/modules-load.d/vergence-i2c.conf).
	modprobe i2c-dev 2>/dev/null || true
	if [ "$UPDATE" != "yes" ]; then
		cat <<'MSG'

Vergence is installed, and nothing is enabled yet (Void's way). Run this once,
as root; it says what each step changes and asks first:

    sudo vergence-setup

It enables seatd, vdm (the login screen and lock), the system bus and polkitd
for drives, Wi-Fi where there is a card and a system log, and adds you to the
seat's group. Then log out and back in, or reboot.

Before removing Vergence later: sudo vergence-setup --undo

MSG
	fi
	;;
esac
